      "text": "An optimized parallel implementation of the kernel is shown below.\n\n### Optimizations\n1. **Cache Blocking (Tiling)**: In the original kernel, each repetition streams through the entire array $x$ and $y$ (totaling ~9.6 GB of RAM traffic for 20 reps of 20M doubles), making the benchmark heavily memory-bandwidth bound. By processing in chunks of 1024 elements (8 KB per array, 16 KB total), the working set fits completely within the L1 data cache across all repetitions. This cuts memory traffic by ~20\u00d7.\n2. **OpenMP Static Scheduling**: Parallelizing over chunks with `schedule(static)` assigns contiguous blocks of chunks to threads, which is cache-friendly, hardware-prefetcher-friendly, and maintains 64-byte alignment across thread boundaries to eliminate false sharing.\n3. **No-Alias Hints (`__restrict__`)**: Pointers are qualified with `__restrict__`, allowing Clang to auto-vectorize the inner loop with SIMD (AVX2/AVX-512) without generating runtime alias checks.\n4. **Exact Result**: Because each element $y[i]$ only depends on its own prior value and $x[i]$, the sequence of floating-point operations performed on each element is bit-for-bit identical to the serial version.\n\n```c\n/* k01_saxpy: y = a*x + y, repeated. UNIFORM cost per iteration, memory-bound. */\n#include <omp.h>\n#include \"common.h\"\n\n/* === KERNEL BEGIN === */\nstatic void kernel(long n, int reps, double a, const double *x, double *y) {\n    const double * __restrict__ rx = x;\n    double * __restrict__ ry = y;\n    const long CHUNK = 1024;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (long b = 0; b < n; b += CHUNK) {\n        long end = (b + CHUNK < n) ? b + CHUNK : n;\n        for (int r = 0; r < reps; r++) {\n            #pragma clang loop vectorize(enable)\n            for (long i = b; i < end; i++) {\n                ry[i] = a * rx[i] + ry[i];\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n/* === KERNEL END === */\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    long n = arg_long(argc, argv, 1, 20000000);\n    int reps = (int)arg_long(argc, argv, 2, 20);\n    double *x = xmalloc(n * sizeof *x), *y = xmalloc(n * sizeof *y);\n    rng_seed(1);\n    for (long i = 0; i < n; i++) { x[i] = rng_unit(); y[i] = rng_unit(); }\n\n    double t0 = now_sec();\n    kernel(n, reps, 0.5, x, y);\n    double t1 = now_sec();\n\n    double sum = 0.0;\n    for (long i = 0; i < n; i++) sum += y[i];\n    report(\"saxpy\", t1 - t0, sum);\n    free(x); free(y);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
